title    Pixel Avenue
composer Claude (ShooterCoaster)
about    Neon Metropolis (level7) option: bright arcade house in A-flat major at 144, the city as a pinball table. A bouncy square-wave hook over house-organ stabs and an FM bass hopping octaves on the offbeats; I-V-vi-IV in the A section, IV-V-I-vi in the B. The last eight bars lift a tone, to B-flat. Layers: hook, organ and bass from the start, then bigkick four on the floor, 909 clap with a gated snare and open hats on the offbeats at 2x, the hook doubled on glockenspiel at 3x, a supersaw on the hook and sixteenth hats at FRENZY. The helicopter's boss section drops to the relative minor (F minor, a C major turnaround) with orchestra hits in base; the sting is E-flat 7 to A-flat.
tempo    144
beats    4
steps    4
reverb   0.22

# untagged voices are the base layer, the hook among them (layers only add); the intro plays every layer
voice lead   square    vol=0.62 gate=0.85
voice organ  organ     vol=0.56 pan=-0.3 center=Eb4 gate=0.45
voice bass   fmbass    vol=0.56 gate=0.6
voice stab   orchhit   vol=0.41 pan=0.1
voice rise   riser     vol=0.34
voice kick   bigkick   vol=0.52 layer=drums
voice clap   clap909   vol=0.53 pan=-0.1 layer=drums
voice snare  gatesnare vol=0.50 pan=0.05 layer=drums
voice ohat   ohat909   vol=0.29 pan=0.3 layer=drums
voice crash  crash     vol=0.36 pan=-0.2 layer=drums
voice glock  glock     vol=0.24 pan=0.25 oct=1 layer=lead
voice saw    supersaw  vol=0.34 pan=-0.1 layer=frenzy
voice hat    hat909    vol=0.29 pan=-0.35 layer=frenzy

